# NOTE: dist/ is intentionally NOT ignored (unlike most Vite projects). This app supports
# a notebook/Git-folder deploy route with no local npm/node available -- if dist/ isn't
# committed, a fresh Git folder clone has no way to produce it. Run `npm run build` and
# commit the updated frontend/dist/ after any change to frontend/src/.

# package-lock.json is intentionally NOT committed here (same reasoning as uv.lock at the
# repo root): this project was originally developed on a machine whose npm is globally
# configured (~/.npmrc) to resolve packages through a Databricks-internal registry proxy
# (npm-proxy.dev.databricks.com) instead of the public npm registry. A lockfile generated
# there records that proxy as every package's source, which is unreachable from outside
# Databricks' network -- silently breaking `npm ci` (and, eventually, `npm install`
# reusing a stale lock) for any external user, undetected until a CI job actually ran
# `npm ci` from outside that network. Use `npm install` (which doesn't require a
# preexisting lockfile) rather than `npm ci` in CI/docs for this project.
package-lock.json

